<3<3 How to install Mandy

This guide assumes that you know what a command-line is and that you know how to use command-line tools. You will need the following command-line tools to be available as commands:

~ <cargo>: Mandy is written in Rust. Cargo is Rust's official package manager. Rust can be installed via RustUp, which can be found >(%[A link to the RustUp page][here][https://rustup.rs])<.
~ <git>: Mandy uses Git to handle version control of its source code. You will need Git to be available from the command-line to install Mandy from its sources via Cargo. Git can be installed by visiting this link >(%[A link to Git's homepage][here][https://git-scm.org])<.

After both of these tools have been installed correctly, Mandy can be installed by running this command: <cargo install --git https://github.com/alyxshang/mandy --branch v.0.1.0>

(^-^)
